0..76 Comment "// A peer that has sent everything before its scope abandons the rest leaves"
77..108 Comment "// the run its clause\'s answer."
109..111 Comment "//"
112..188 Comment "// The run\'s scheduler starts a fork\'s child when the root first waits. Here"
189..261 Comment "// the child sends both payloads and ends before the clause abandons the"
262..277 Comment "// root\'s rest."
278..280 Comment "//"
281..357 Comment "// The root takes the first payload, then the exit abandons its continuation"
358..434 Comment "// with the second payload still on the channel. No cancellation reaches the"
435..473 Comment "// ended peer, so the run answers `7`."
474..476 Comment "//"
477..552 Comment "// - see: #3305 — the cancellation hop, which a peer still waiting at the"
553..575 Comment "//   abandonment needs"
576..647 Comment "// - see: Fowler, Lindley, Morris and Decova, _Exceptional Asynchronous"
648..725 Comment "//   Session Types_, POPL 2019, doi:10.1145/3290341 — cancellation reaching"
726..739 Comment "//   the peer"
741..819 Comment "/// The peer sends both payloads and ends before the clause abandons the rest."
